{"fieldId":null,"choiceId":null,"choiceName":null,"criteria":"A document is relevant (Responsive) if it relates to: (1) the City of Atlantis RFP for the municipal energy project, including bids, proposals, or contract negotiations; (2) BigThorium’s process for bidding on contracts, where the City of Atlantis project or related practices are discussed; (3) discussions among BigThorium employees or agents about giving gifts, incentives, luxury goods, or other benefits as part of the bid or contract process; (4) discussions about bribing, influencing, or otherwise improperly inducing City of Atlantis officials or other public officials connected to the municipal energy project; (5) communications about BigThorium winning, seeking to win, or securing the City of Atlantis contract; (6) purchase, reimbursement, or delivery records for luxury goods or unusual payments that could function as bribes; (7) use of third-party intermediaries, consultants, or agents in connection with the City of Atlantis opportunity; or (8) communications between City of Atlantis officials and BigThorium representatives regarding the RFP, contract, or related matters. Documents are also relevant if they show intent to influence the award, internal discussions of unethical practices, or awareness of anti-bribery laws and compliance issues tied to this project.

A document is generally non-relevant if it: (1) concerns unrelated projects, customers, or RFPs not involving the City of Atlantis municipal energy project; (2) discusses routine business operations, HR matters, or financial issues with no connection to gifts, bribes, or the City of Atlantis contract; (3) involves marketing, sales, or procurement activities unrelated to public officials or the disputed project; or (4) references “RFP” in a different context not tied to the City of Atlantis solicitation. Purely technical Relativity training materials or administrative review logistics, absent case-specific content, are also non-responsive.

Privilege status (attorney-client, work product, confidential) does not determine responsiveness; privileged documents can still be responsive if they meet the above criteria.","issuesFieldId":null,"issues":null}
